# Subagent orchestration

This repo is a npm workspaces monorepo: `backend`, `frontend`, `bot`, `packages/shared`.

## Default specialists

| Subagent | Own |
| --- | --- |
| `/planner` | Cross-package plans (readonly) |
| `/prisma-db` | `backend/prisma`, migrations, generate scripts |
| `/shared` | `@language-turtle/shared` under `packages/shared/` |
| `/backend` | Express API under `backend/src`, backend tests |
| `/frontend` | React UI under `frontend/` |
| `/telegram-bot` | Telegraf bot under `bot/` |
| `/reuse-auditor` | Find duplication / missed reuse (readonly) |
| `/component-reuse` | Extract/reuse React components and UI hooks |
| `/dry-refactor` | Extract functions, remove duplicate logic, tidy modules |
| `/verifier` | Post-implementation checks |

## Delegation rules

1. Multi-package or unclear scope → start with `/planner`, then follow its order.
2. Schema or migration needed → `/prisma-db` before feature code.
3. Cross-package types/constants/contracts → `/shared` before consumers (`backend` / `frontend` / `telegram-bot`).
4. Keep each specialist inside its folder boundaries; do not ask backend to edit React pages.
5. Typical feature order: `prisma-db` → `shared` → `backend` → `frontend` / `telegram-bot` → `verifier`.
6. Cleanliness / DRY: `/reuse-auditor` first (findings), then `/dry-refactor` and/or `/component-reuse`; if a shared contract is needed, `/shared` before consumers.
7. After non-trivial work → `/verifier` with an explicit claim list.
8. Parallelize only independent packages (e.g. frontend UI polish + bot copy) after prisma/shared contracts are stable.

## Explicit invokes

Users may call `/backend`, `/frontend`, `/telegram-bot`, `/prisma-db`, `/shared`, `/planner`, `/reuse-auditor`, `/component-reuse`, `/dry-refactor`, `/verifier` directly.
